invariant: INV-14
file: srv_resume.c
catches: srv_flight_test
reason: the server accepts the ticket it selected without checking the client's
  binder, which RFC 9846 §4.3.11 makes a MUST before accepting a PSK
  (rfc9846.txt:2541-2544). The binder is what ties the ticket to this
  ClientHello, so without it anyone who replays a captured ticket gets a
  resumed handshake started, and a client whose PSK does not match gets
  as far as the Finished. test/srv_resume_tests.h offers a binder one bit
  off and requires decrypt_error.

--- old
    return equal != 0;
}
--- new
    (void)equal;
    return 1;
}
